    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe endpoint is `POST /api/owners`, served by OfficeFloor function pipelines; the response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct. I added `riskFlag` as a **derived** field (like `identityKey`, `ownerSegment`, `telephoneDisplay`), computed from the owner's already-stored fields so it is recomputed identically on every read.\n\n`riskFlag` is true when **any** of the three signals hold:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 the stored `possibleDuplicate` flag (set by `FlagPossibleDuplicate`: soft soundex+postcode match).\n2. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 the stored `capacityWarning` flag (set by `FlagCapacityWarning`: city already holds 40+ owners, the soft threshold below the hard 50 limit).\n3. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 the email's second-level label matches a known disposable provider (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) but under a non-blocked TLD. (Exactly-blocked `.com` domains are rejected 400 by `RequireEmailDomain` and never persisted, so a *stored* such email is by definition adjacent, not blocked.)\n\n### Changes\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean (`readOnly`) property to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets `getRiskFlag`/`setRiskFlag`.\n- **`mapper/RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 standalone helper `RiskFlag.of(owner)` computing the OR of the three signals, kept out of the mapper interface so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping method (matching `OwnerSegment`/`Locality`).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` expression mapping.\n\n### Tests\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` (a fully-unique owner with no email \u2192 false) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` with no regressions.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's \"disposable-adjacent\" wasn't previously defined anywhere in the code (the existing blocklist is for the hard 400 rejection). I defined it as \"shares a known disposable provider's second-level label under a non-blocked TLD\" and documented that precisely in both the schema description and the helper Javadoc \u2014 if you had a different notion of \"adjacent\" in mind (e.g. Levenshtein distance to a blocked domain, or a broader keyword set), that's the one spot to adjust.",
